WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:10.368
The father's tie color is an important cue for guests to tell which side of the family he's from.

2
00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:25.512
The standard is blue tones (sky blue, navy, purple, gray) for the groom's father, and red tones (pink, magenta, red, orange) for the bride's father.

3
00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:35.280
With a dark navy suit especially, a bright pink or sky-blue tie adds a fresh, trustworthy accent.

4
00:00:35.616 --> 00:00:45.864
Tie patterns can range from solid to sharp stripes or dots, but the one thing to avoid is a black tie.

5
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.504
It evokes funeral attire and can dampen the celebratory mood.

6
00:00:51.840 --> 00:01:00.648
A tie matched to the father's personal color, chosen to brighten his face the most, completes a stylish look.

7
00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:08.880
Gold or silver ties are also an option — a plain, pattern-free style keeps those looking sharp.
